title HUNK2 — a decoded image meets Skate; lit pixels reach the canvas
prompt Autonomous loop: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates. (Continuing from HUNK1, shipped this session.)
think HUNK1 landed and shipped; the quest doc's named next crux is HUNK2 — the decoded grid meets Skate, a bounded down-map from RGBA pixels to Skate's palette-indexed cell grid, proven on metal (lit pixels reach the canvas). Ungated, agent-doable, high-Lindy (the paint seam beneath both the parts marketplace and the Photos app).
think Studied brushstroke/skate_grid.rye: a Grid holds cells (glyph bytes) parallel to fg_index (per-cell palette slot), a bounded palette of 8 slots (0 = sentinel, 1..7 real colors), and rasterize/lit_pixel_count. Skate only lights glyph pixels, and the extended_glyphs seam (its ZETA4 emoji atlas) renders cell values 128..255 — so a full-block atlas makes each cell paint as a solid color block. Placed the bridge in brushstroke/ (Skate's home) and symlinked qoi.rye in, so both imports resolve locally.
think Design decision recorded in the module header: a fixed seven-color anchor palette (cube corners + black/white) that block averages quantize to by nearest squared distance. A richer image-derived palette is a later rung; the crux here is a bounded, deterministic, spatial down-map that reaches the canvas. Integer partition of the image into cols×rows blocks counts every pixel once; sums fit u32 (255·2^20 < u32 max); both grid axes bounded at construction.
think Wrote down_map: init the grid, set the 7 palette slots, average each block, pick the nearest slot, set the cell to the block glyph and its fg_index to the slot. Selftest crafts a red-left/blue-right 8×8 image, down-maps to 2×2, and proves color reached the right cells (red→slot 3, blue→slot 5), determinism (a second map is byte-identical), and that the rasterized canvas carries the real colors with lit pixels present. Empty image and over-ceiling grid refuse by name.
obs First run panicked on assert(lit == total): a full-block glyph is 8×8 but a Skate cell is 8×16, so each cell's lower half stays background — the honest count is one 8×8 glyph square per cell (cols·rows·(8·scale)²), which I asserted exactly rather than claiming the whole canvas. A correctness catch the witness earned.
obs TAME caught five compound asserts (channel-bound, slot-bound, block-nonempty, and the two color reads); split each so the failing half names itself, then GREEN. Width clean. No breach rename, so no cairn; no gate crossed (no network, key, or funds).
loom witness=hunk_skate_witness grid=2x2 canvas=16x32 lit_pixels=256 anchors=7
